Subject: [PATCH] mmc: dw_mmc: arm software DTO on SDIO writes too

dw_mci_set_drto() was only called for DW_MCI_RECV_STATUS. A CMD53 write
that finishes the command (CMD_DONE) but never raises DATA_OVER therefore
sits in STATE_SENDING_DATA / STATE_DATA_BUSY with no software timer and
no hardware DTO. mmc_wait_for_req() waits forever.

Observed 2026-09-03 on Stamp-P4 Image b4575e14 leftover rst after SSH
exec true: CMD53_BB VALID cmd_arg=0x97ec0000 cmd_done=1 idmac=1
data_over=0 dto=0 end=0. idsts=NI|TI.

The existing dto_timer already completes such a wait by synthesizing
SDMMC_INT_DRTO. Arm it for SEND the same way as RECV.

Signed-off-by: EasyStick <dev@localhost>
---
diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/dw_mmc.c
@@ -2164,11 +2164,11 @@
 			if (!test_and_clear_bit(EVENT_XFER_COMPLETE,
 						&host->pending_events)) {
 				/*
-				 * If all data-related interrupts don't come
-				 * within the given time in reading data state.
+				 * DATA_OVER / XFER_COMPLETE can also fail to
+				 * arrive on a write (IDMAC TI latched, no DTO).
+				 * Recv-only arming left that wait unbounded.
 				 */
-				if (host->dir_status == DW_MCI_RECV_STATUS)
-					dw_mci_set_drto(host);
+				dw_mci_set_drto(host);
 				break;
 			}
 
@@ -2203,12 +2203,10 @@
 		case STATE_DATA_BUSY:
 			if (!dw_mci_clear_pending_data_complete(host)) {
 				/*
-				 * If data error interrupt comes but data over
-				 * interrupt doesn't come within the given time.
-				 * in reading data state.
+				 * Same write-side hole as STATE_SENDING_DATA:
+				 * without DATA_OVER the request never ends.
 				 */
-				if (host->dir_status == DW_MCI_RECV_STATUS)
-					dw_mci_set_drto(host);
+				dw_mci_set_drto(host);
 				break;
 			}
 
@@ -4293,6 +4293,9 @@ static void dw_mci_dto_timer(struct timer_list *t)
 		 * we should notify the driver to terminate current transfer
 		 * and report a data timeout to the core.
 		 */
+		dev_err(host->dev,
+			"EASYSTICK_MMC TX_DRTO state=%d dir=%u\n",
+			host->state, host->dir_status);
 		host->data_status = SDMMC_INT_DRTO;
 		trace = dw_mci_cmd53_trace_active(host);
 		if (trace)
